  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -53,6 +53,11 @@ display or *TShark* output.  For example, a protocol is semantically\n equivalent to the sequence of bytes that it spans, not its displayed text\n in the protocol tree.\n \n+Many operators have English forms; the English forms are given in lower case\n+in this documentation but are case-insensitive. In contrast, the names of fields,\n+functions, and macros are case-sensitive, as are the first characters in\n+escape sequences.\n+\n === Comparison operators\n \n The comparison operators can be expressed either through English-like\n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "doc/man_pages/wireshark-filter.adoc",
      "old_path": "doc/man_pages/wireshark-filter.adoc",
      "a_mode": "100644",
      "b_mode": "100644",
      "new_file": false,
      "renamed_file": false,
      "deleted_file": false,
      "generated_file": false
    },
    {
      "diff": "@@ -543,6 +543,8 @@ A complete list of available comparison operators is shown in <<DispCompOps>>.\n [TIP]\n ====\n English and C-like operators are interchangeable and can be mixed within a filter string.\n+Beginning in Wireshark 5.0, the English forms of operators (but not field, function, or\n+macro names, or the first characters in escape sequences) are case-insensitive.\n ====\n \n [#DispCompOps]\n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "doc/wsug_src/wsug_work.adoc",
      "old_path": "doc/wsug_src/wsug_work.adoc",
      "a_mode": "100644",
      "b_mode": "100644",
      "new_file": false,
      "renamed_file": false,
      "deleted_file": false,
      "generated_file": false
    },
    {
      "diff": "@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ The following changes have been made since version 4.7.1:\n   Follow Stream is implemented. wsbuglink:20610[].\n   Export Objects is implemented.\n   Request/response tracking is implemented.\n+* Display filter operators' English forms like \"and\" and \"or\" are case-insensitive.\n \n The following changes have been made since version 4.7.0:\n \n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "doc/Wireshark_Release_Notes.adoc",
      "old_path": "doc/Wireshark_Release_Notes.adoc",
      "a_mode": "100644",
      "b_mode": "100644",
      "new_file": false,
      "renamed_file": false,
      "deleted_file": false,
      "generated_file": false
    },
    {
      "diff": "@@ -58,6 +58,12 @@\n  */\n %option extra-type=\"dfsyntax_t *\"\n \n+/*\n+ * Token matching is case-insensitive. yytext still has the original case.\n+ * The escape sequences are the only patterns not case-insensitive.\n+ */\n+%option case-insensitive\n+\n %{\n /*\n  * Wireshark - Network traffic analyzer\n@@ -325,7 +331,7 @@ HexExponent\t\t([pP][+-]?[[:digit:]]+)\n \t}\n }\n \n-<DQUOTE>\\\\x[[:xdigit:]]{1,2} {\n+<DQUOTE>\\\\(?-i:x)[[:xdigit:]]{1,2} {\n \t/* hex sequence */\n \t/*\n \t * C standard does not place a limit on the number of hex\n@@ -342,8 +348,8 @@ HexExponent\t\t([pP][+-]?[[:digit:]]+)\n \t}\n }\n \n-<DQUOTE>\\\\u[[:xdigit:]]{0,4} {\n-\t/* universal character name */\n+<DQUOTE>\\\\(?-i:u)[[:xdigit:]]{0,4} {\n+\t/* universal character name, BMP */\n \tupdate_string_loc(yyextra, yytext);\n \tif (yyextra->raw_string) {\n \t\tg_string_append(yyextra->quoted_string, yytext);\n@@ -355,8 +361,8 @@ HexExponent\t\t([pP][+-]?[[:digit:]]+)\n \t}\n }\n \n-<DQUOTE>\\\\U[[:xdigit:]]{0,8} {\n-\t/* universal character name */\n+<DQUOTE>\\\\(?-i:U)[[:xdigit:]]{0,8} {\n+\t/* universal character name, upper-case (8 digits) */\n \tupdate_string_loc(yyextra, yytext);\n \tif (yyextra->raw_string) {\n \t\tg_string_append(yyextra->quoted_string, yytext);\n",
      "collapsed": false,
